---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About Ynvesters – AI Tools Discovery & Comparison"
  description="Ynvesters is an independent editorial site dedicated to helping professionals cut through the noise and find the AI tools that actually work."
>
  <div style="max-width: var(--max-width); margin: 0 auto; padding: 3rem 1.5rem;">
    <h1 style="font-size:2rem; font-weight:800; margin-bottom:0.5rem;">About Ynvesters</h1>
    <p style="color:var(--color-text-muted); margin-bottom:2.5rem; font-size:1.1rem;">
      Independent reviews and comparisons of AI tools — no hype, no paid placements.
    </p>

    <section style="margin-bottom:2.5rem;">
      <h2>Our Mission</h2>
      <p>
        The AI software landscape changes faster than anyone can track. New tools launch daily, pricing shifts overnight,
        and last month's market leader is often replaced by a better alternative before you've even finished evaluating it.
      </p>
      <p>
        Ynvesters exists to give professionals a reliable, up-to-date reference. We publish in-depth reviews,
        side-by-side comparisons, and practical how-to guides so you can make confident decisions without
        spending hours on research yourself.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section style="margin-bottom:2.5rem;">
      <h2>Who We Are</h2>
      <p>
        Ynvesters is run by an independent editorial team based in Asia, with hands-on backgrounds in software
        development, content production, and digital product evaluation. We use the tools we write about —
        on real accounts, with real prompts — before a single sentence goes to publication.
      </p>
      <p>
        We do not accept sponsored reviews, affiliate placements, or early access arrangements that come with
        editorial strings attached. If a tool has a meaningful weakness, we document it. If a cheaper alternative
        outperforms a category leader, we say so.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section style="margin-bottom:2.5rem;">
      <h2>How We Test</h2>
      <p>
        Our testing process is hands-on and documented. Here's exactly what that means in practice:
      </p>
      <ul style="line-height:2.2;">
        <li><strong>Real accounts, real prompts.</strong> We create actual accounts — typically on free tiers to reflect the experience most new users have — and run identical or comparable prompts across competing tools to make direct comparisons fair.</li>
        <li><strong>Screenshots as evidence.</strong> Every test we run is captured with screenshots at the time of testing. Claims about output quality, generation speed, UI behavior, and tool responses are backed by images taken during live sessions, not reconstructed from memory.</li>
        <li><strong>Measured timing.</strong> When we report generation speed — "under one second," "approximately 3 minutes" — those are observed, real-time measurements, not estimates from marketing copy.</li>
        <li><strong>Output evaluation criteria.</strong> We assess writing tools on: prompt fidelity (did it do what was asked?), output usability (could this go live without editing?), and differentiation (does it do something competitors don't?).</li>
        <li><strong>Pricing verified at time of publication.</strong> All pricing figures are pulled directly from official pricing pages on the date the article is published or last updated. We link to source pages so you can verify current rates.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Recent examples of hands-on tests documented in our articles: Grammarly vs. Hemingway Editor tested on
        identical text (91/100 vs. Post-graduate readability rating); Canva Magic Write generating an Instagram
        caption in under one second; Replit Agent building a fully functional todo app with PostgreSQL persistence
        in just over 3 minutes; Perplexity AI returning 20 cited sources vs. Google AI Overview returning 9 on
        the same query.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section style="margin-bottom:2.5rem;">
      <h2>What We Cover</h2>
      <ul style="line-height:2;">
        <li>AI coding assistants, writing tools, image generators, and productivity apps</li>
        <li>Head-to-head comparisons with objective, testable criteria</li>
        <li>Pricing breakdowns — including free tiers, limits, and hidden costs</li>
        <li>Step-by-step tutorials for getting real value out of new tools</li>
        <li>Analysis of major AI product launches and what they mean in practice</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section style="margin-bottom:2.5rem;">
      <h2>Editorial Standards</h2>
      <p>
        Every factual claim in our articles is sourced from official documentation or a verifiable third-party
        reference. We link directly to primary sources — official product sites, GitHub repositories, academic
        papers — so you can verify anything we write.
      </p>
      <p>
        Articles are updated when products change significantly. If you find an error or outdated information,
        please <a href="/contact">contact us</a> with a source link and we'll correct it within 48 hours.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section style="background:var(--color-bg2); border:1px solid var(--color-border); border-radius:10px; padding:1.5rem 2rem;">
      <h2 style="margin-top:0;">Advertising Disclosure</h2>
      <p style="margin-bottom:0;">
        Ynvesters displays advertisements served by Google AdSense. Ad revenue helps us keep the site free and
        updated. Advertisers have no influence over our editorial coverage — our reviews and recommendations
        are written independently. For more information, see our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
